  partName: Exhaust Manifold
  description: The Exhaust Manifold, positioned at the middle-center-rear of the
    Hover Engine, is an elongated component that collects exhaust gases from the
    engine's cylinders and directs them towards the exhaust system. Its medium size
    and standard surface material enable efficient exhaust gas flow and heat management.
    Interestingly, the Exhaust Manifold's design must balance exhaust gas flow rates
    with thermal stress and vibration considerations to ensure optimal engine performance.
